{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Acid Squelch",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: the rubbery, screaming acid line of acid house and acid techno: a resonant filter squelching on every note, sliding between some of them, the cutoff slowly drifting as if a hand were on the knob.\n\nHow it's built: Clock 1/16 \u2192 Sequencer \u2192 Slew (the slides) \u2192 a saw, an octave down. The Ladder filter at -24 dB with RESONANCE high; a short envelope and a slow LFO are mixed into its CUTOFF (the envelope squelches each note, the LFO plays the knob for you). Drive after the filter for grit; a delay for space. Hold a key around C3 and the line plays from it (it plays from C3 until you do).\n\nTweak: RESONANCE (the scream), the filter's CV (how far each note squelches), the envelope's DECAY, the Slew's times (longer slides), the LFO's RATE; turn the LFO's mixer level down and play CUTOFF yourself.",
